# Photoshop Frontend — React & UI Conventions

## Components
- Functional components only — no class components
- Props interfaces must be defined and exported alongside the component
- Destructure props in the function signature, not inside the body
- Components longer than 120 lines should be split into sub-components

## Hooks
- Custom hooks must be prefixed with `use` and live in a hooks/ directory
- API calls belong in custom hooks, never directly in component bodies
- Always provide cleanup functions in useEffect when subscribing to events or timers
- Loading, error, and success states must all be handled — no silent failures

## State Management
- Lift state to the nearest common parent — avoid prop drilling beyond 2 levels
- Use useCallback for event handlers passed to child components
- Derived values should be computed with useMemo, not stored in state

## Styling
- Use CSS modules or Tailwind utility classes — no inline style objects for layout
- All interactive elements must have visible focus indicators for accessibility
- Image previews must include alt text derived from the filename or user-provided label
